{%- comment -%}
  Outputs ONE word: the shipping group a product belongs to.

      {%- capture ship_group -%}{%- render 'shipping-class', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}

  This snippet and 'shipping-group' are the only two files in the theme that know a ship:*
  tag exists. Everything else — the buybox, the card badge, the cart, the structured data —
  asks here instead of testing tags itself. Before that, six files each carried their own
  copy of the same if/elsif chain, so adding a shipping group meant finding all six and
  changing a rate meant finding the four that quoted it.

  The tags come from content/freight.json and are written by CoreYard during the publish
  that creates the product, so a part is never live wearing the wrong one. scripts/
  check_contracts.py verifies the group ids and tags below still match that file.

  The ids are pickup | freight299 | freight199 | ground44 | ground34 | ground29 | ground24 |
  ground19 | ground14 | ground9 | free. They are STABLE IDENTIFIERS, not rate declarations:
  they travel in the hidden _ship cart line property and sit inside shopper carts right now,
  so renaming one would make an in-flight cart fall back to the free-shipping wording. If a
  rate changes, change the rate in 'shipping-group' and in content/freight.json; leave the
  id alone.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign group = 'free'
  if product.tags contains 'ship:pickup-only'
    assign group = 'pickup'
  elsif product.tags contains 'ship:freight-299'
    assign group = 'freight299'
  elsif product.tags contains 'ship:freight-199'
    assign group = 'freight199'
  elsif product.tags contains 'ship:ground-44'
    assign group = 'ground44'
  elsif product.tags contains 'ship:ground-34'
    assign group = 'ground34'
  elsif product.tags contains 'ship:ground-29'
    assign group = 'ground29'
  elsif product.tags contains 'ship:ground-24'
    assign group = 'ground24'
  elsif product.tags contains 'ship:ground-19'
    assign group = 'ground19'
  elsif product.tags contains 'ship:ground-14'
    assign group = 'ground14'
  elsif product.tags contains 'ship:ground-9'
    assign group = 'ground9'
  endif
  echo group
-%}
